    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2d5d6b096cc8f47e22725198037485c6194759321c4a891f0f7df41f50f9ae96",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source gives zeta two distinct physical roles: at the Bose critical point, unit effective fugacity evaluates the phase-space polylogarithm as zeta(d/2), whose pole at d=2 is a condensation obstruction in the stated approximation; separately, exchanging thermal and finite-size Euclidean channels equates a continuum free energy with a regularized discrete-mode Casimir energy and yields the completed-zeta reflection relation. Their conjunction supports a contrast between representations, not a common physical derivation.",
