    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_d5dc95f513e7b3770f3d53c5b53311dc7de50e3d0ed316f0779ff47a561e0e17",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Under a constant scattering kernel, the momentum-dependent saddle equation collapses to a scalar effective-fugacity fixed point; specializing to two dimensions makes that fixed point algebraic and organizes pressure through the Rogers dilogarithm, while changing statistics alters the real-domain branch behavior and a coupling matrix extends the construction to jointly solved mixed-species fugacities with additive pressure contributions.",
